; openapi-typescript (7.x) declares a peer of typescript ^5.x, but this scaffold is deliberately on
; TypeScript 6 (see tsconfig.json / package.json). The tool generates correctly against TS 6 — only its
; published peer range lags the release. legacy-peer-deps lets `npm ci` install it without an ERESOLVE
; rather than downgrading the whole project for one build-time codegen tool's stale peer declaration.
; Scope is this leaf client only; the .NET side is unaffected. Revisit when openapi-typescript widens its peer.
legacy-peer-deps=true
